00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:47,040
Thanks for your help.

2
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:53,040
[Episode 22]
[Severe Withdrawal]

3
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:18,200
<i>We're running out of time. Eat up.
Or you'll be late for school.</i>

4
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:20,360
<i>Sweetie, listen.</i>

5
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:23,040
<i>- You can't just eat meat and skip the veggies.
- Why not?</i>

6
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,439
<i>If so, you won't be able to, you know, go.</i>

7
00:03:26,439 --> 00:03:27,839
<i>I go just fine!</i>

8
00:03:27,839 --> 00:03:30,180
<i>Come on, yesterday you were straining.</i>

9
00:03:45,599 --> 00:03:47,119
Dad.

10
00:03:47,119 --> 00:03:49,040
I'm going out.

11
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,640
Don't worry.

12
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:40,980
Mr. Fu, everyone's here. Let's get started.

13
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,400
I will now announce the disciplinary decision

14
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:07,239
regarding the improper use
of deceleration equipment

15
00:05:07,239 --> 00:05:12,159
on Hengshi Air Flight 5123,
Rong City to Jiang City, on July 21, 2025.

16
00:05:12,159 --> 00:05:17,239
During the flight, the captain in command,
Yue Yang, suffered a sudden incapacitation.

17
00:05:17,239 --> 00:05:19,064
First Officer...

18
00:05:29,719 --> 00:05:33,960
First Officer Ruan Si Xian declared Mayday
and performed the landing.

19
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:37,799
After touchdown, reverse thrust
was retracted earlier than the prescribed time,

20
00:05:37,799 --> 00:05:42,560
creating a risk of runway excursion
under adverse weather conditions.

21
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:45,960
Ruan Si Xian failed to conduct a
comprehensive assessment of weather conditions,

22
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:50,039
thereby placing the lives and property
of the passengers on board at risk.

23
00:05:50,039 --> 00:05:55,540
In summary, Hengshi Air will issue
a suspension of flight duties

24
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:59,060
to Ruan Si Xian.

25
00:06:05,799 --> 00:06:09,799
Hengshi Air Safety Committee,

26
00:06:09,799 --> 00:06:14,120
August 3rd, 2025.

27
00:07:05,599 --> 00:07:07,120
What's with that look on your face?

28
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:10,039
Nothing. Nothing at all.

29
00:07:10,039 --> 00:07:12,599
What should we do next?

30
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:14,599
I don't know.

31
00:07:14,599 --> 00:07:17,919
- Maybe keep the distance?
- "Keep the distance"?

32
00:07:17,919 --> 00:07:20,600
Speed up the reform process!

33
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,819
Right, the reform process.

34
00:07:28,599 --> 00:07:30,879
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

35
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:42,039
Captain Yue, are you feeling better?

36
00:07:42,039 --> 00:07:43,639
Much better.

37
00:07:44,719 --> 00:07:46,540
It's just...

38
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:50,599
I didn't expect this to cause so much trouble.

39
00:07:50,599 --> 00:07:52,279
Glad you're recovered.

40
00:07:52,279 --> 00:07:54,080
Health is what matters most.

41
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,839
Yeah.

42
00:07:55,839 --> 00:07:59,999
- If there's nothing else, I'll get going.
- Actually, there is.

43
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,160
Go ahead.

44
00:08:04,799 --> 00:08:06,780
Well,

45
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:10,039
I've talked to the Safety Committee about this.

46
00:08:10,039 --> 00:08:15,919
But they just told me to rest and recover,
and they'd handle the investigation.

47
00:08:15,919 --> 00:08:20,919
I never expected them to investigate
and end up with this result.

48
00:08:20,919 --> 00:08:22,719
I'm truly sorry.

49
00:08:22,719 --> 00:08:24,399
You don't need to apologize to me.

50
00:08:24,399 --> 00:08:27,279
And if you feel the result is unfair,

51
00:08:27,279 --> 00:08:29,780
- you can file an appeal.
- I can't do that.

52
00:08:31,479 --> 00:08:34,239
This is a company-wide decision.

53
00:08:34,239 --> 00:08:37,800
If I were to appeal,
I'd be going against the airline.

54
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:41,920
I don't want to, and I don't dare to.

55
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:44,440
Then why are you telling me all this?

56
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,719
Partly an apology.

57
00:08:47,719 --> 00:08:49,280
But I also need to explain.

58
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:53,479
What happened that day was a sudden emergency.

59
00:08:53,479 --> 00:08:56,040
I had no control over it.

60
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:59,400
And now the whole company is blaming me.

61
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,859
I feel...

62
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,380
wronged.

63
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:12,320
So, you feel wronged.

64
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:15,800
Is that why you asked me here today?

65
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:18,780
- To vent your frustrations?
- More like to open up.

66
00:09:19,479 --> 00:09:22,879
Because I feel like our recent experiences
have been similar.

67
00:09:22,879 --> 00:09:27,960
Look, we've both hit problems at work
and in our personal lives too.

68
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:31,440
I've already made things clear
with Jiang Zi Yue.

69
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,680
And you and Mr. Fu...

70
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:36,719
Actually, about you and Mr. Fu,

71
00:09:36,719 --> 00:09:39,020
I have something to say.

72
00:09:39,719 --> 00:09:44,680
You know, if two people want to last,
first they need to be well-matched.

73
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,479
Then there's family, education, background,

74
00:09:46,479 --> 00:09:48,440
- shared interests--
- Captain Yue.

75
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:51,119
My relationship with Fu Ming Yu
is a private matter.

76
00:09:51,119 --> 00:09:52,800
We had an amicable breakup,

77
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:56,920
and it seems to have nothing to do with
what we're talking about today.

78
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:57,960
No, it doesn't.

79
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:02,080
But I don't want to see a pretty girl
waste her time, you know?

80
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:03,680
Honestly,

81
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:10,519
you are a pilot
with a great image, ability, and potential.

82
00:10:10,519 --> 00:10:11,999
I really admire you.

83
00:10:11,999 --> 00:10:13,080
And I like you too.

84
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,479
I mean, a beautiful girl like you...

85
00:10:14,479 --> 00:10:17,519
Everyone feels like getting closer
to a pretty girl, right?

86
00:10:17,519 --> 00:10:19,280
But I have my principles.

87
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:24,879
If anything I did before
made you uncomfortable, I apologize.

88
00:10:24,879 --> 00:10:26,639
I'm sorry.

89
00:10:26,639 --> 00:10:31,839
So if there's anything you need on this matter,
I can take responsibility.

90
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:34,540
Because I do have a sense of responsibility.

91
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:48,260
First of all,

92
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:52,400
I didn't do this for you,

93
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,200
and I don't need anyone
to take responsibility for me.

94
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,939
Second...

95
00:11:00,359 --> 00:11:02,239
Forget it.

96
00:11:02,239 --> 00:11:03,979
That's all.

97
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:10,719
Well, since we've gotten this far,
let me ask you one more thing.

98
00:11:10,719 --> 00:11:12,440
I've been wanting to ask this for a while.

99
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:16,239
Jiang Zi Yue and I ended up like this.

100
00:11:16,239 --> 00:11:18,709
Does it have anything to do with you?

101
00:11:28,359 --> 00:11:30,060
Captain Yue,

102
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:38,358
about why you and Jiang ended up like this,
you know better than anyone, don't you?

103
00:11:40,599 --> 00:11:44,200
You brought up responsibility just now,

104
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:48,080
so you should know
that as the captain in command,

105
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,839
if you had any sense of responsibility,

106
00:11:49,839 --> 00:11:53,320
you wouldn't have stayed silent
and refused to face it.

107
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:59,280
And whether in relationships or at work,

108
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:05,380
in my view,
you've got zero sense of responsibility.

109
00:12:09,743 --> 00:12:12,920
I haven't touched this coffee.

110
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:16,076
You ordered it, so you take care of it.

111
00:12:44,599 --> 00:12:46,680
Yang, if you're not feeling well,
go to the restroom.

112
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,920
Go cough it up properly.

113
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:51,239
You're making noise every few seconds.

114
00:12:51,239 --> 00:12:56,200
If my hand slips,
do you have any idea how bad things would be?

115
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,979
- How bad?
- It'll be done for.

116
00:13:02,119 --> 00:13:04,979
I'm done for.

117
00:13:10,182 --> 00:13:12,119
What's this?

118
00:13:12,119 --> 00:13:13,599
- Photocard decorating.
- What?

119
00:13:13,599 --> 00:13:16,699
Photocard decorating. It's a handicraft.

120
00:13:19,719 --> 00:13:21,719
Then why are our faces on them?

121
00:13:21,719 --> 00:13:25,467
Because I ship you two.
I'm a shipper of Ruan Si Xian and you.

122
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,440
What does that mean?

123
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:31,960
It means she's a loyal fan
who supports you two being together.

124
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,813
They're upside down.

125
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:40,440
Where did you get the photos?

126
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:43,800
I took yours without you noticing.

127
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,479
"Captain" Ruan has photos online,

128
00:13:45,479 --> 00:13:50,280
so I downloaded them and made stickers.

129
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:52,979
Should I be praising your dedication?

130
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,599
Sit down.

131
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,440
What are these even for?

132
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,187
Nothing practical.

133
00:14:03,187 --> 00:14:08,759
Just commemorating my favorite couple
that broke up.

134
00:14:08,759 --> 00:14:11,660
Hoping they'll get back together someday.

135
00:14:18,119 --> 00:14:20,160
I let the snacks slide,

136
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:23,239
but now you're sitting here
making these at work.

137
00:14:23,239 --> 00:14:26,239
If someone else walks in,
how am I supposed to explain this?

138
00:14:26,239 --> 00:14:29,320
Never mind whether it makes me
look like an incompetent manager.

139
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:32,479
Won't everyone think I'm some lovesick idiot?

140
00:14:32,479 --> 00:14:34,560
- Yes.
- "Yes"?

141
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,219
No, you're not a lovesick idiot.

142
00:14:38,839 --> 00:14:40,759
Confiscated.

143
00:14:40,759 --> 00:14:42,780
Mine too. Here.

144
00:15:04,599 --> 00:15:05,999
Hello, here are your snacks.

145
00:15:05,999 --> 00:15:07,519
Thank you.

146
00:15:07,519 --> 00:15:10,648
Xuan, where's my sister?

147
00:15:26,519 --> 00:15:29,160
Sister, don't be sad.

148
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:34,519
I know you've lost a lot,
but you have to remember, you've always got us.

149
00:15:34,519 --> 00:15:36,920
We'll always have your back.

150
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:40,119
What are you doing?
Watch out, my clothes will be stained.

151
00:15:40,119 --> 00:15:41,900
What's up with you?

152
00:15:42,519 --> 00:15:44,119
Wait.

153
00:15:46,359 --> 00:15:47,759
You're not crying?

154
00:15:47,759 --> 00:15:48,800
Why would I be crying?

155
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:51,639
You got grounded, you went through a breakup,

156
00:15:51,639 --> 00:15:53,380
and you're not crying?

157
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,760
Have some duck necks.

158
00:16:01,479 --> 00:16:06,120
If you look at it that way,
getting grounded isn't so bad after all.

159
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:09,199
I'm stealing a sip of your unlimited drink.

160
00:16:10,479 --> 00:16:13,739
Easy on that. You're a lightweight.

161
00:16:14,479 --> 00:16:17,400
I thought you'd be a complete mess.

162
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,840
I had a whole speech prepared to cheer you up.

163
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,080
Guess you don't need it.

164
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:23,519
Cheer up about what?

165
00:16:23,519 --> 00:16:24,759
I'm quite happy.

166
00:16:24,759 --> 00:16:27,839
I finally get my mentor now.

167
00:16:27,839 --> 00:16:32,280
When it comes to life,
the outcome doesn't matter that much.

168
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:36,119
When I watched those passengers
getting off the plane safely,

169
00:16:36,119 --> 00:16:38,920
I wanted to high-five every single one of them.

170
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:42,839
What's more, that night,
I got to see my friends and family again.

171
00:16:42,839 --> 00:16:46,680
In that moment,
I felt like it was all worth it.

172
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,920
Whatever the outcome, I can handle it.

173
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:53,040
I went to the airport that night too,
but I was stuck outside.

174
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:55,359
Did my brother-in-law tell you?

175
00:16:55,359 --> 00:16:57,099
Brother-in-law?

176
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,579
Former brother-in-law.

177
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:04,401
I'm renovating my hotel,
and I'm short on funds,

178
00:17:04,401 --> 00:17:06,239
so I have to keep the sweet talk going.

179
00:17:06,239 --> 00:17:08,200
How much did he give you to win you over?

180
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,479
Money isn't the point.

181
00:17:09,479 --> 00:17:12,160
The point is, family helps each other out.

182
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:13,999
Family?

183
00:17:13,999 --> 00:17:16,999
- You and him are family?
- What are you talking about?

184
00:17:16,999 --> 00:17:19,640
You and I are family.

185
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,239
Since when are we family?

186
00:17:21,239 --> 00:17:22,400
When did this happen?

187
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:26,079
The night your plane almost went down,
the whole family was worried sick.

188
00:17:26,079 --> 00:17:27,920
Mom scalded her foot

189
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,840
and still rushed to the airport
in the pouring rain, wearing slippers.

190
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:33,980
That's a really hurtful thing to say.

191
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,039
She scalded her foot?

192
00:17:39,039 --> 00:17:40,840
I told her to sit down and rest,
but she wouldn't.

193
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:43,039
She said when you were little,

194
00:17:43,039 --> 00:17:46,960
she always had to be the first one
at the kindergarten gate to pick you up.

195
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:51,740
So that night, she wanted you to see her
the moment you got off the plane.

196
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:56,500
<i>Auntie Dong. Over here.</i>

197
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:07,759
Sister, there's always been a room for you
at home.

198
00:18:07,759 --> 00:18:10,360
I thought you'd come live with us.

199
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,479
I was nervous back then.

200
00:18:12,479 --> 00:18:15,759
My grandmother said once you came,
my dad wouldn't love me as much anymore.

201
00:18:15,759 --> 00:18:18,239
That was not what I cared about.

202
00:18:18,239 --> 00:18:21,740
I was just afraid that once you came,

203
00:18:24,759 --> 00:18:27,099
I'd lose my mom again.

204
00:18:31,999 --> 00:18:38,719
That sounds selfish,
but she's such an amazing mom.

205
00:18:38,719 --> 00:18:41,462
I never met my own mother.

206
00:18:42,279 --> 00:18:44,579
She passed away during childbirth.

207
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:48,319
I don't know what it feels like
to be loved by a mom.

208
00:18:48,319 --> 00:18:50,920
Then Mom came,

209
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:55,260
and I always felt like part of her love for me

210
00:18:56,239 --> 00:18:59,740
was really meant for you.

211
00:19:00,799 --> 00:19:07,320
But that night, for the first time,
I understood what a mother's love feels like.

212
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:10,559
She stood there the whole night

213
00:19:10,559 --> 00:19:12,960
waiting for news
that your plane had landed safely.

214
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:18,680
She couldn't even stand on her own.
My dad and I had to hold her up on either side.

215
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:24,220
When I touched her hand, it was freezing cold.

216
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,040
And I thought,

217
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:37,283
was it this cold
the last time my own mother touched me?

218
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:47,239
Why are you telling me all this?

219
00:19:47,239 --> 00:19:49,339
No use pretending.

220
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,519
You two clearly care about each other.

221
00:19:52,519 --> 00:19:53,880
Why are you so stubborn?

222
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,659
I'm not stubborn.

223
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:01,659
I'm used to being alone.

224
00:20:03,999 --> 00:20:06,640
You're not used to being alone.

225
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:10,440
You're used to pushing everyone away
when things get hard.

226
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:13,506
Isn't that what you did
with Fu Ming Yu this time?

227
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:21,780
Eat. You talk too much.

228
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:40,200
Good morning, board members
and department heads.

229
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:44,319
Today we are holding the 11th meeting
since the QAR reform began two years ago.

230
00:23:44,319 --> 00:23:49,360
This reform has been difficult and lengthy,
but it is crucial to Hengshi Air.

231
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:52,200
The QAR is an objective record of
pilots' actual flights,

232
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:56,400
allowing us to identify systemic issues
through big data

233
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:59,179
and improve the company's safety quality...

234
00:24:21,559 --> 00:24:25,105
- Hurry up.
- Do you have to move it yourself? Let me.

235
00:24:38,999 --> 00:24:42,339
Put the painting here. In the center.

236
00:25:59,719 --> 00:26:01,160
One order of cold noodles, please.

237
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:03,500
Got it. Coming right up.

238
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:19,319
Welcome. We saved the quietest rooms for you.

239
00:26:19,319 --> 00:26:21,239
You'll sleep great tonight.

240
00:26:21,239 --> 00:26:23,120
Check them in.

241
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:24,840
Hello.

242
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:28,279
Regarding the handling of lithium battery smoke
and fire emergencies on our aircraft,

243
00:26:28,279 --> 00:26:31,880
the first thing is to follow the golden rule:
flying the aircraft is the first priority.

244
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:34,160
If necessary, transfer controls
to the crew member

245
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:36,301
on the side opposite the fire.

246
00:26:36,301 --> 00:26:38,360
[Flight Schedule]

247
00:26:38,360 --> 00:26:39,640
Here it comes.

248
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:41,640
- Everyone, look up.
- So beautiful.

249
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:43,519
- Come on.
- Look this way.

250
00:26:43,519 --> 00:26:44,520
- Come on.
- Take a photo.

251
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:46,400
Look over there.

252
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:48,000
Come on.

253
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:50,640
Take one for me too.

254
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:52,960
- Come on.
- My eyes were closed. One more.

255
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:55,300
One, two, three.

256
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:05,289
You should get along well with the purser.

257
00:27:11,079 --> 00:27:13,200
So much for our morning session.

258
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,880
Please head to the cafeteria for lunch.

259
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:16,999
We'll resume an hour later.

260
00:27:16,999 --> 00:27:18,878
Thank you for your hard work.

261
00:27:22,559 --> 00:27:25,680
Mr. Fu, Chairman Fu just called
to ask about the meeting.

262
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:27,940
Would you like to call him back now?

263
00:27:28,559 --> 00:27:31,719
Let's not tell him until we have results.

264
00:27:31,719 --> 00:27:33,319
Understood.

265
00:27:38,079 --> 00:27:39,719
Thanks.

266
00:27:39,719 --> 00:27:42,460
I didn't expect you to show up today.

267
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:46,479
What do you mean by that?

268
00:27:46,479 --> 00:27:49,160
I'm here representing Bo'ao Air.

269
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:51,519
I never slack off on work.

270
00:27:51,519 --> 00:27:53,419
Don't start with that.

271
00:27:57,279 --> 00:28:01,079
Honestly though, I don't get it.

272
00:28:01,079 --> 00:28:02,559
Why go against these people?

273
00:28:02,559 --> 00:28:05,280
Is the reform of flight quality monitoring
necessary?

274
00:28:05,280 --> 00:28:08,039
It's a lot of work with nothing to show for it.
Why bother?

275
00:28:08,039 --> 00:28:12,540
Besides, these people
are a bunch of stuck-in-the-mud relics.

276
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:14,479
You can't beat them.

277
00:28:14,479 --> 00:28:17,999
Whether I can beat them or not,
I'll have to try.

278
00:28:17,999 --> 00:28:21,680
Besides, these rules have been in place
for over 20 years.

279
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:26,260
Many don't match today's aircraft
and flight technology anymore.

280
00:28:29,999 --> 00:28:31,360
Is there a hidden motive?

281
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:34,060
Are you trying to win back Ruan Si Xian?

282
00:28:40,559 --> 00:28:42,159
Yes.

283
00:28:42,799 --> 00:28:44,759
Then why go through all this trouble?

284
00:28:44,759 --> 00:28:46,400
Let me help you out.

285
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:48,640
I have years of experience in this.

286
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:54,640
When a girl's mad, whatever the reason,
you'll never figure out what you did wrong.

287
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:58,680
The only thing you need to do is kiss her.

288
00:28:58,680 --> 00:29:01,279
Kiss her like you mean it. Kiss her like crazy.
Kiss her, and you're done.

289
00:29:01,279 --> 00:29:05,419
Only after you kiss her will you understand
that girls love that.

290
00:29:08,759 --> 00:29:11,200
- Are you done?
- No.

291
00:29:12,160 --> 00:29:14,020
Don't be late.

292
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:49,999
I've mentioned that QAR is an objective record
of pilots' actual flights,

293
00:29:49,999 --> 00:29:53,960
allowing us to identify systemic issues
through big data

294
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:56,440
to improve our company's flight safety quality.

295
00:29:56,440 --> 00:30:01,200
In the early days, it did play a positive and
constructive role in standardizing operations.

296
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:02,680
But in recent years,

297
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:06,120
there's been an increasing tendency to
use punishment as a substitute for management.

298
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:08,920
It has become a tool for going after pilots.

299
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,719
I wonder if any of you have felt this way.

300
00:30:10,719 --> 00:30:12,160
Its impact...

301
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:14,279
<i>Everything is ready.</i>

302
00:30:14,279 --> 00:30:16,600
<i>Amazing!</i>

303
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:18,840
<i>Make sure everything is set up.</i>

304
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:20,920
<i>Tonight's make-or-break.</i>

305
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:22,719
...the runway edge light incident.

306
00:30:22,719 --> 00:30:25,719
<i>- Okay.</i>
- What do these incidents tell us?

307
00:30:25,719 --> 00:30:26,840
- They all point to one thing.
<i>- Good luck.</i>

308
00:30:26,840 --> 00:30:28,279
The management of the QAR...

309
00:30:28,279 --> 00:30:31,220
<i>- I'll be right there.</i>
- ...has put the cart before the horse.

310
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:48,479
We're running out of time.
How's everything coming along?

311
00:30:48,479 --> 00:30:49,620
Almost done.

312
00:30:49,620 --> 00:30:53,479
- Who did the drinks? They're not right.
- I did. What's wrong with them?

313
00:30:53,479 --> 00:30:56,680
Come on, it's a proposal, a joyous occasion.
You didn't make a heart shape?

314
00:30:56,680 --> 00:30:59,120
Don't you think heart shapes are a bit tacky?

315
00:30:59,120 --> 00:31:01,160
I want a heart shape. Tacky is fine.

316
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:03,360
You know a heart shape
is an upside-down butt, right?

317
00:31:03,360 --> 00:31:04,440
Spare me the details.

318
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:09,300
We're running out of time.
Do it. Make me a butt shape.

319
00:31:10,079 --> 00:31:15,120
Dong, we need to push all the instruments
back a bit and leave more space, okay?

320
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:16,360
We've got a problem.

321
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:17,361
Someone's at the door.

322
00:31:17,361 --> 00:31:18,960
Looks like Zheng You An.

323
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,279
- She's onto us?
- What should we do?

324
00:31:20,279 --> 00:31:24,120
- Stop her. Quick.
- Xuan, get me a drink.

325
00:31:24,120 --> 00:31:25,680
You An! What a coincidence.

326
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:28,120
I'm going to the beach for some juice.

327
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:29,360
Let's go together. Come on.

328
00:31:29,360 --> 00:31:30,960
The beach at this hour?

329
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:32,920
It's way too sunny. Let's drink here.

330
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,400
Well, look.

331
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:37,559
My new dress. Pretty, right?
Take a couple of photos for me?

332
00:31:37,559 --> 00:31:41,200
- It's pretty. I'll do it after I have a drink.
- Now, please.

333
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:45,239
Si Xiao Zhen, you're acting really weird today.

334
00:31:45,239 --> 00:31:47,139
What's over there?

335
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:52,759
Xuan,

336
00:31:52,759 --> 00:31:55,120
owner of the pub,

337
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:58,519
your business is expanding.

338
00:31:58,519 --> 00:32:00,940
You're even doing weddings now.

339
00:32:02,680 --> 00:32:06,360
I have a friend who...

340
00:32:06,360 --> 00:32:08,120
Stand up straight.

341
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:09,960
Si Xiao Zhen, go.

342
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:11,840
Everyone, stop.

343
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:13,440
Stand up.

344
00:32:14,279 --> 00:32:15,920
Stand straight.

345
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:21,920
First you make me do full makeup,
then you tell me to dress up nice.

346
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:28,160
What, is my "casual friend"
about to propose to me?

347
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,200
No, not that.

348
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:31,400
You said it yourself. He's a casual friend.

349
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:32,799
I'm really good at keeping secrets.

350
00:32:32,799 --> 00:32:34,600
I have to keep it for my client.

351
00:32:34,600 --> 00:32:35,880
I won't say a word.

352
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:37,799
- Right.
- Fine.

353
00:32:37,799 --> 00:32:40,640
But to be honest,

354
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:46,200
this whole thing you're doing with Yan An
is way too tacky.

355
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:48,859
Yeah, I do think so.

356
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:57,443
So, do you want to follow my lead
and make this proposal a lot more interesting?

357
00:33:03,120 --> 00:33:05,260
That's all I have to say.

358
00:33:06,380 --> 00:33:08,519
Let's take a break.

359
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:14,200
Come on. Come here.

360
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:16,479
Finally, you're done.

361
00:33:16,479 --> 00:33:18,560
Come to the pub with me later.

362
00:33:18,560 --> 00:33:21,799
It's my lifelong event.
Tonight's make-or-break.

363
00:33:21,799 --> 00:33:25,239
You can see how busy I am.
I don't have time for your personal affairs.

364
00:33:25,239 --> 00:33:26,719
Come on, Fu Ming Yu.

365
00:33:26,719 --> 00:33:28,200
We've been friends for so many years.

366
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:30,559
Think about all the times
I've helped you out. Do the math.

367
00:33:30,559 --> 00:33:32,719
I need you this once.
Are you going to bail on me?

368
00:33:32,719 --> 00:33:37,360
Look, man. You can see I'm in no mood for this.

369
00:33:37,360 --> 00:33:39,468
Ruan Si Xian will be there.

370
00:33:55,759 --> 00:33:56,920
My dear friends,

371
00:33:56,920 --> 00:34:00,719
we have only this one chance,
so please keep sharp. Got it?

372
00:34:00,719 --> 00:34:01,920
- Stay sharp!
- On it.

373
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,799
When You An gets here,
don't fuss with these things anymore.

374
00:34:03,799 --> 00:34:04,880
Let's all gather over here.

375
00:34:04,880 --> 00:34:07,960
- Don't worry.
- The music needs to build from soft to strong.

376
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:09,519
Really set the mood.

377
00:34:09,519 --> 00:34:10,720
Please.

378
00:34:10,720 --> 00:34:12,599
And the petals.
Make sure they're falling everywhere.

379
00:34:12,599 --> 00:34:13,920
- Blissful, you hear me?
- No problem.

380
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,039
- Got it?
- No problem.

381
00:34:15,039 --> 00:34:17,240
Fu Ming Yu, you...

382
00:34:17,240 --> 00:34:18,920
You're useless.

383
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:20,360
Anyway, the atmosphere has to be right.

384
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:21,800
You got it.

385
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:23,199
This isn't a drill, friends.

386
00:34:23,199 --> 00:34:25,800
Keep sharp. When You An walks in,
make her feel like a princess.

387
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:28,119
Petals everywhere, and everyone moves in.

388
00:34:28,119 --> 00:34:30,199
Everyone, heads up. She's coming!

389
00:34:30,199 --> 00:34:32,179
- Hurry!
- Go!

390
00:34:36,119 --> 00:34:39,579
False alarm. It's Ruan.

391
00:34:40,320 --> 00:34:42,420
Scared me.

392
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:50,079
When You An comes in, you know what to say.

393
00:34:50,079 --> 00:34:51,720
- Will do.
- Quick! Look over here.

394
00:34:51,720 --> 00:34:53,320
Easy.

395
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:57,400
This is not a drill.

396
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:59,360
- It's the real deal!
- She's coming!

397
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:00,960
She's here!

398
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:48,540
I never expected this. I'm so touched.

399
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:54,159
Zheng You An.

400
00:35:54,760 --> 00:35:56,940
Are you impressed?

401
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:05,159
- Impressed.
- Do you like it?

402
00:36:05,159 --> 00:36:08,219
I do.

403
00:36:17,479 --> 00:36:19,139
Zheng You An,

404
00:36:20,639 --> 00:36:22,299
marry me.

405
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:30,199
Marry him!

406
00:36:30,199 --> 00:36:31,280
Marry him!

407
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:32,320
Marry him!

408
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:34,219
Marry him!

409
00:36:38,519 --> 00:36:40,079
Yan An.

410
00:36:40,079 --> 00:36:41,679
I'm here.

411
00:36:42,720 --> 00:36:44,320
I...

412
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:51,099
I won't.

413
00:36:52,720 --> 00:36:54,519
Can you stop doing things
that only make yourself feel good?

414
00:36:54,519 --> 00:36:57,199
Think about what I want.

415
00:36:57,199 --> 00:36:59,280
Also, are these real flowers?

416
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:01,720
How much did you spend?
Can you please save some money?

417
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:04,960
Take them back to my hotel later.

418
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:07,599
Friends, you didn't come here
for nothing today.

419
00:37:07,599 --> 00:37:09,400
It's been a while
since we all got together like this.

420
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:13,519
Let's treat tonight like a party, okay?

421
00:37:13,519 --> 00:37:15,559
- Okay!
- All right then.

422
00:37:15,559 --> 00:37:17,920
Mr. Yan, everyone's in a good mood.

423
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:19,679
How about we take a group photo?

424
00:37:19,679 --> 00:37:21,320
Let's do that. Photo first.

425
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:22,880
Come on. Let's take a photo.

426
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:24,240
Come on.

427
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:26,199
Take a photo. Come here.

428
00:37:26,199 --> 00:37:28,199
Photo time, you two.

429
00:37:28,199 --> 00:37:30,079
Use my tripod. You press the shutter for us.

430
00:37:30,079 --> 00:37:32,559
- Do you know how?
- How can you do this to me?

431
00:37:32,559 --> 00:37:34,579
Stand still. Be good.

432
00:37:42,599 --> 00:37:45,800
Check the shot. Are we all in the frame?

433
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:47,039
Yes.

434
00:37:47,039 --> 00:37:48,760
Smile, everyone.

435
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:50,159
Three.

436
00:37:50,159 --> 00:37:51,440
Two.

437
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:53,040
One.

438
00:38:15,039 --> 00:38:16,639
Yan An,

439
00:38:18,360 --> 00:38:20,519
between us,

440
00:38:20,519 --> 00:38:23,519
you're always the one who gives more.

441
00:38:23,519 --> 00:38:29,760
You're not creative,
but you always try to give me surprises.

442
00:38:29,760 --> 00:38:36,720
I know you're not confident about
whether we can last.

443
00:38:36,720 --> 00:38:38,600
But you know what?

444
00:38:38,600 --> 00:38:44,099
Every time I hit a rough patch,
you're the one right there beside me.

445
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:53,079
Yan An, I have a long-term
partnership plan for us.

446
00:38:53,079 --> 00:38:55,039
Are you interested?

447
00:38:55,039 --> 00:38:57,060
I am!

448
00:39:00,159 --> 00:39:03,799
Let's get married, Yan An!

449
00:39:05,639 --> 00:39:11,200
- Say yes!
- Say yes!

450
00:39:11,200 --> 00:39:14,960
- Say yes!
- Say yes!

451
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:16,980
I do.

452
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:22,139
- Which hand?
- This one.

453
00:39:26,559 --> 00:39:28,299
Where's mine?

454
00:39:31,639 --> 00:39:33,239
Hurry up.

455
00:39:35,599 --> 00:39:37,599
You bought such a big one.

456
00:39:37,599 --> 00:39:41,179
Kiss!

457
00:41:12,280 --> 00:41:16,000
I've got the photos from last time.

458
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:19,280
Want to take a look?

459
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:20,880
Pick one.

460
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:30,670
Tonight was pretty dramatic.

461
00:41:30,670 --> 00:41:32,720
Did you know about the plan?

462
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:33,960
No.

463
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:35,360
Neither did I.

464
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:37,460
I didn't even know you were coming.

465
00:41:38,920 --> 00:41:43,060
So if you'd known I was coming,
would you not have come?

466
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:54,280
Yan An said you've been busy
and wouldn't come to his proposal.

467
00:41:54,280 --> 00:41:56,540
I wasn't planning to come,

468
00:41:58,679 --> 00:42:00,659
but he said you'd be there,

469
00:42:01,240 --> 00:42:03,179
so I came.

470
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:15,639
By the way, I bought a house.

471
00:42:15,639 --> 00:42:17,659
Your family's old house?

472
00:42:21,272 --> 00:42:23,000
Congratulations.

473
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:24,920
You finally got what you wanted.

474
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:29,440
I should've saved more before buying it,
but I was afraid it'd be too late.

475
00:42:29,440 --> 00:42:31,920
The old house could be demolished any time.

476
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:34,479
I was afraid that by the time I saved enough,
it'd be gone.

477
00:42:34,479 --> 00:42:36,139
What about us?

478
00:42:45,599 --> 00:42:48,679
I must say, this one turned out pretty good.

479
00:42:48,679 --> 00:42:49,800
I'll take this one.

480
00:42:49,800 --> 00:42:53,079
You keep it.

481
00:42:53,079 --> 00:42:55,520
You know what I want to ask.

482
00:42:55,520 --> 00:42:58,199
It doesn't matter.

483
00:42:58,199 --> 00:43:02,900
What matters is that you're doing well
and not working too hard.

484
00:43:03,599 --> 00:43:07,800
About the reform, if it's really too difficult,
then let it go.

485
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:11,840
I've only recently realized
that in the adult world,

486
00:43:11,840 --> 00:43:14,200
things are not simply about yes or no.

487
00:43:14,200 --> 00:43:16,920
Many things have their own trajectory.

488
00:43:16,920 --> 00:43:21,779
You even have to take detours
to reach some goals.

489
00:43:22,639 --> 00:43:25,840
But thankfully, in this world,

490
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:29,540
as long as you keep moving forward,
there will always be a way.

491
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:38,360
Keep it.

492
00:43:38,360 --> 00:43:40,060
Look forward.

493
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:45,040
I'm almost home. Bye.

